// src/v4/test/claim/impossible_bug/idempotency_contract.dag
//
// Scope: TestClaim — idempotency-contract violation impossible-bug class
//        (R1). There is NO @idempotent annotation: idempotence is a DERIVED
//        algebraic property. An operation whose structural position requires
//        idempotence (it inhabits an idempotent algebraic structure per
//        std/algebra.dag) but whose composition lens/idempotency.dag derives
//        as non-idempotent (Witness::Violates) MUST error at compile time.
//        The requirement is inhabitance; the violation is lens-derived;
//        neither is a tag (feedback_no_annotations — compositional only).
// Anchor: THESIS.md "Enumerable impossible-bug classes" §377-378 R1 — the
//         CLASS only; THESIS's "marked @idempotent" wording is annotation
//         shorthand, the modeled mechanism is algebra-inhabitance + lens
//         derivation (the lens reads Node structure, never a tag). Also
//         lens/idempotency.dag.
//
// Owns:
//   - test_nonidempotent_in_idempotent_position_caught: TestClaim
//     - input: an operation declared to inhabit an idempotent algebraic
//       structure (std/algebra.dag) whose body composes a non-idempotent
//       effect (e.g. external-state mutation)
//     - expected: Diagnostic { reason: IdempotencyViolation,
//       correction: Correction, at: <inhabitance / non-idempotent-compose> }
//   - test_idempotent_inhabitant_passes: TestClaim
//     - input: an operation in the same idempotent-algebra position whose
//       structure lens/idempotency.dag derives as idempotent → compiles
//
// Consumes:
//   - std/verification.dag, std/diagnostic.dag, std/algebra.dag, lens/idempotency.dag
//
// Status: scaffold — fill per TASKS.md T-14
// Brief: see BRIEF_TEMPLATE.md.

module v4.test.claim.impossible_bug.idempotency_contract

